  m_Text: Every power station, from hydroelectric dams to wind turbines and nuclear
    plants, generates electricity using electromagnetic induction. Instead of moving
    a magnet by hand, large turbines rotate powerful magnets or coils at high speeds
    to produce the electricity that powers homes and cities.
