    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: The induced voltage in a coil depends on how quickly the magnetic flux
    changes. A faster-moving magnet, a stronger magnetic field, or more turns in
    the coil all increase the induced voltage.
