    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 0
    m_MaxSize: 300
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: Lenz's Law states that the induced current always flows in a direction
    that opposes the change in magnetic flux that produced it. As a magnet moves
    toward or away from a coil, the induced current creates its own magnetic field.
    This induced magnetic field resists the change by opposing the magnet's motion.
    If the direction of the magnet is reversed, the direction of the induced current
    also reverses.
--- !u!222 &1542251065
